# Do not add `.github` here.
#
# The `dev` stage's test suite asserts on the workflow files.  `tests/unit/test_rpm_spec.py`
# resolves `.github/workflows/packaging.yml` from `Path(__file__).parents[2]`, which inside the
# container is `/app`, and `docker-compose.yml`'s dev service has no bind mount, so `/app` is
# this build context and nothing else.  Excluding `.github` makes those tests error at fixture
# setup with `FileNotFoundError`.
#
# The shipped image is unaffected, which is why this is safe: the `runtime` stage does
# `COPY --from=build /app/.venv.container` and copies no source at all, so `.github` cannot reach
# a published image.  The cost is only that editing a workflow invalidates the `COPY . .` layer
# and re-runs `uv sync` -- cheap, because that step is uv-cache-mounted.

.env
.venv*
.tox

__pycache__/
*.py[oc]

.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache

.coverage
cov_report.xml

build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
out/
rpmbuild/
